      "side": 1,
      "message": "(Jumping in because Firas pinged me)\n\nFrom the [release note](https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/main/doc/releases/release-notes-3.7.rst#id175) CONFIG_PTHREAD_KEY is renamed to CONFIG_POSIX_THREADS, so yes I think they refer to the same thing.\n\nBut the original comment also mentioned that `BoringSSL stores one pointer per thread`, if this comment is still valid, you\u0027ll need `HEAP_MEM_POOL_ADD_SIZE_BORINGSSL` for these pointers.",
