      "side": 1,
      "message": "I have a question:\n- Is my understanding correct. Every time we need to store a pointer returned in thread local data, we need to allocate a new `struct pthread_key_data` using k_malloc?\n- Are we assuming here that BoringSSL is the only library that calls `pthread_setspecific()` to store a pointer in thread local data? Is this the reason why we enabled the POSIX_THREADS config to begin this i.e. only for the purpose of handling the BoringSSL requirement?",
      "parentUuid": "dbaaa396_b67aa6c9",
      "revId": "cf4bdd7e67446a3bbf9582950f93f4bd7e3fc7e8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
